@@ -9,6 +9,18 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## View cache
+
+Astro's client router retains up to five visited page views in a persistent DOM
+container. Returning to a cached pathname and query string reuses the existing
+nodes, including their local UI state. Inactive views are hidden and inert; the
+least recently visited view is removed when the limit is reached. Sign-in and
+sign-up views opt out with `cacheView={false}` so their forms are removed on exit.
+Navigation still fetches the destination through Astro to update its head,
+styles, and scripts. Reloading the page clears the view cache.
+
+Run the DOM lifecycle tests without a browser or server with `pnpm test`.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
